#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:28
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "How an L3 FHIR Implementation Guide is authored in FSH, built with SUSHI, the validator and the IG Publisher, reviewed and published, starting from a source model that is ready. Generic: what produces the source model is the layer above's own process, which maps its model and then calls Process_L3Fhir. This one names no such model. folio-assistant — the generic L3 FHIR IG pipeline. Source of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other BPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it by `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG. The <bootstrap.processes:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill that implements it; <cat-harness.processes:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared work plan in beans/."
msgstr ""

