msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:69
#. Diagram label
msgid "Source model ready"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:42
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Task_AuthorFsh is the single re-entry point for both failure paths in this diagram — an invalid-FHIR loop from Gateway_Valid with no record left behind, and a QC failure that arrives only after Task_QcBeans has filed it — so the lane has to be able to tell a mechanical re-run from a finding that needs to be read, and the diagram gives it no other signal than which edge fired."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:70
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The IG's source model is ready: l3-fhir-authoring's required sourceModel. Which model, and how it was produced, is the calling process's to say — this pipeline names none, because L3 is derived and the layer above owns what it is derived from."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:63
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The last lane and the only one with no path back into the loop — reaching it means Task_IgPublisher already succeeded on Lane_Qc's clean verdict. It does not itself decide whether the release is authorised: that call is draft-to-publication.bpmn's, and Task_PublishIg only executes what that separate process has already cleared."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:106
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The QC reviewer rules on the aggregate QA against the publication gates. Emitting the QA report is mechanical; ruling on it is a decision, which is why it sits in the reviewer's lane rather than the build's."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The single gate between a syntactically valid FHIR JSON and the full IG Publisher build — Task_IgPublisher runs only once this lane says clean, so a QC finding here is what keeps a compiling-but-wrong profile from ever reaching a publishable IG rather than being caught only after the whole site is built."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:49
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Two different jobs share this lane rather than one continuous run. Task_Sushi and Task_Validate turn FSH into validated FHIR JSON and loop straight back to the modeller lane on failure with no bean filed — re-running compile-and-validate is cheap enough that a durable finding would be noise. Task_IgPublisher is the other job, reached only once Lane_Qc has passed, and its output is what Lane_PubMgr actually publishes."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:91
#. Diagram label
msgid "Validate against profiles [fhir-validation]"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:92
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Validate the compiled resources against their profiles and the packages they constrain. A validator that could not start is could-not-determine, never a pass with an empty findings list. Failures return to authoring."
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:23
#. Diagram label
msgid "Work plan (beans)"
msgstr ""

#: ../fhir-harness/processes/content/l3-fhir-pipeline.bpmn:74
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Write the FSH profiles, value sets and definitions the source model calls for. This is the stage where profiles, slicing and invariants belong — a decision that can only be expressed in FHIR comes here, not back into the source model."
msgstr ""

